<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie0bf530571e39c0514a1bd5721e0ead8217a0805" commit="7ce777c3730ff7a4391ee82bb30b2a619a9b7974" commit_message="Add message for Hammer firmware updater use.  This CL adds the boot message for hammer firmware update. When the hammer needs update at boot time, then we show the message before entering UI.  BUG=b:65180379 TEST=With new firmware, plug hammer and reboot poppy,      check the boot message shows up. CQ-DEPEND=CL:651788  Change-Id: Ie0bf530571e39c0514a1bd5721e0ead8217a0805 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/656859 Commit-Ready: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Joel Kitching &lt;kitching@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="656859" owner_email="akahuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/assets" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/assets" ref="refs/changes/59/656859/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If5324c036faa8a7520f06945871a0d1b602d4da3" commit="5d02a3b4e12e753e996d6b7fae1619e913b238fc" commit_message="hammerd: Force update at boot and show boot message during update.  On boot, we try to update several kinds of firmware. If the firmware needs to update, we block the UI at until update finishes, and then go back to Chrome UI. Therefore, we need a new upstart job to check these jobs sequentially.  This CL adds a job &quot;boot-update-firmware&quot; for this. It triggers hammerd and show up the message if the hammer firmware needs update.  When the base does not need to update (firmware is up to date, or the base is not attached), the task only takes 0.06 second. It does not affect the bootup time significantly.  BUG=b:65180379, chromium:764232 TEST=With new firmware, plug hammer and reboot poppy,      check the boot message shows up and      keyboard works after entering UI TEST=With original firmware, plug hammer and reboot poppy,      check the boot message does not show up, enter UI directly TEST=With new firmware, unplug hammer and reboot poppy,      check the boot message does not how up, enter UI directly.      Then plug hammer, check the keyboard works after 5 seconds. CQ-DEPEND=CL:651711,CL:656859  Change-Id: If5324c036faa8a7520f06945871a0d1b602d4da3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/651788 Commit-Ready: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="651788" owner_email="akahuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="26" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/88/651788/26" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iaf2c02c3398898610d018394ccc8aceb407a4cf1" commit="9f19398c8d3f8b56149bee45728b3440315e9441" commit_message="hammerd: install required shell script.  Because the logic of hammerd-pre-ui.conf is complicated, we implement it in a shell script. This CL installs all shell scripts in hammerd/init into /usr/share/cros/init.  BUG=b:65180379 TEST=emerge-poppy hammerd CQ-DEPEND=CL:651788  Change-Id: Iaf2c02c3398898610d018394ccc8aceb407a4cf1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/651711 Commit-Ready: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chih-Yu Huang &lt;akahuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="651711" owner_email="akahuang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/11/651711/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iab87ba2ef306fa7fa4a9777282246324560e70d4" commit="ef07a7c9793ca78b61653eceb7f084b2bea25e90" commit_message="Remove unused Android M toolchain packages  We no longer build anything for Android M, so let's drop all the dead M-specific packages from portage.  BUG=b:67434102 TEST=Trybot (dead code)  Change-Id: Iab87ba2ef306fa7fa4a9777282246324560e70d4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/702115 Commit-Ready: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Benjamin Gordon &lt;bmgordon@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="702115" owner_email="tfiga@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/15/702115/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I32070d598f699b5fa49dc67ec1223be2131317fd" commit="380229cace11ce649e699ffed9d3d30dc72b4de5" commit_message="sys-devel/arc-build: Remove support for Android MNC  Remove code that is unused since we stopped building for Android MNC. While at it, fix the global &quot;use&quot; logic by moving it to src_install, according to portage guidelines.  BUG=b:67434102 TEST=cros tryjob for kevin-release, elm-release and eve-release  Change-Id: I32070d598f699b5fa49dc67ec1223be2131317fd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/702116 Commit-Ready: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Tomasz Figa &lt;tfiga@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="702116" owner_email="tfiga@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromium